/-!
# Suzuki calculations for both component orbits in 13.8.16

The concrete natural Suzuki module has only scalar commuting binary
endomorphisms. For the two-factor product, every commuting endomorphism is
scalar on each factor. The odd field exponent excludes a nonidentity
commuting operator whose order divides a product of powers of two and three.
The accompanying reduction keeps central extensions and proves the commutator contradiction on the whole
required module.

The source assembly still needs the invariant Borel and its component
centralization, and the occurrence and equivariant transport of the natural
central sections from the genuine F.9.18 alternatives. These calculations
do not assert either part of 13.8.16 before those inputs are discharged.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
13.8.16, printed pp.952–953, with F.9.18(4–7), printed pp.325–326.
-/
